  assets:{score:18,rationale:'The saved r6 keeps the 28 native editable leaves: enamel casing, narrow rim highlight, bevel, twelve radial ticks, two highlighted hands and brass pivot. The material hierarchy is legible on dark and bright real backgrounds. It remains intentionally restrained vector material, so this score does not claim photoreal texture.'},
  adaptation:{score:18,rationale:'Seven independent measured inputs cover English month, Chinese duration, Chinese deadline, explicit no-time negative, bright plant-room English “good time”, dense Chinese temporal list and a separate scheduling cue. Actual production has six positive groups and one zero-overlay negative; the main exact Application includes two live-action backgrounds and audio-only stress cases. A separate portrait Application/production is recorded with a warm-room source and a 3:4 no-time negative; it is not silently folded into this exact score.'},
  editability:{score:9,rationale:'The saved style has 28 editable leaves and the new hold is available at Definition/Application/Element precedence levels with backward-compatible omission. Existing r5 UI edit/restore remains valid; the r6 change is a single native field and usage-guide update. Common-pivot geometry remains encoded in editable per-leaf motion channels.'},
  evidence:item.previews.map(p=>({fixture:p.fixture,sha256:p.sha256})),
  inspection:'Frame-based inspection only: seven published r6 MP4s, full event strips for six positive groups, explicit no-time negative, native plan boundaries, six positive durations measured at 0.65/0.66/0.92/1.00/1.48/0.65s, and a separate portrait production. The dense input uses one selected merged semantic range; raw three-event repetition is retained as a boundary stress record. Native source audio streams and decode validation are present. No continuous video playback viewing or listening performed.',
  limitations:'This score applies only to saved clock r6 and the exact 1280×720/30fps main Application (scale 0.4, center 0.875,0.25) plus its seven listed measured inputs. It is not a universal family score, not a claim of automatic semantic detection, and not a claim of listening or continuous playback. The clock is a qualitative time cue, never a real-time reading or countdown. Further positions, tiny scale, dense unrelated cues, long-form caption combinations and continuous audiovisual review remain outside this record. The portrait production is evidence for a separate Application, not inherited by the main score.',
